{
    double carPrice = 3000;
    double clothesPrice = 100;
    double bookPrice = 20;

    double adjustedCarPrice = AdjustCarPrice(carPrice, clothesPrice, bookPrice);
    Console.WriteLine("Adjusted car price: " + adjustedCarPrice);
}
```

The output will be:

```
Adjusted car price: 6000
```

So, the final cost of the purchase after adjusting the car price would be:

$6000 (adjusted car price) + $100 (clothes price) + $20 (book price) = $6120

Note: This solution assumes that the input prices are valid and non-negative. You may want to add additional checks or handle invalid inputs appropriately in a real-world application.

